I can help — this is a good start. Before I make specific suggestions, a couple quick clarifying questions (they affect what to ask and what tests to request):

- Do you have a diagnosis of type 2 diabetes already? If so, what is your most recent A1c and any diabetes meds (metformin, insulin, SGLT2 inhibitors, GLP-1 agonists, etc.)?  
- Can you confirm the INR value — did you mean 3.20 (not 320)? Are you on warfarin or another anticoagulant?  
- Which medications do you actually take for hypertension and anemia? (You listed omeprazole and calcium + vitamin D — omeprazole is for acid reflux and Ca/D are not anemia therapy, so I want to be sure I understand your current meds.)  
- Any current joint pain or mobility limitations that make you worry about orthopedics?

If you want, I can draft an email to Dr. Jennifer Lee with the questions below once you confirm those details. Meanwhile, here are focused question lists and a visit checklist you can use for your annual physical.

Questions about type 2 diabetes screening/management (or if you already have diabetes, to review control and complications)
- Do I have diabetes (if not diagnosed) or prediabetes based on my labs? Should we check an A1c today?  
