4) Questions and checklist about a referral to Northwest Orthopedics
When to consider referral:
- Persistent or progressive joint pain (hip, knee, shoulder, spine) that limits daily activities or sleep despite conservative care
- Recurrent falls, instability, or marked loss of mobility
- Suspected or known advanced osteoarthritis on prior imaging
- Prior traumatic injury with ongoing dysfunction
