- Red flags that make referral more appropriate
  - Persistent or worsening joint pain that limits activities or sleep
  - Mechanical symptoms (locking, catching), instability, or deformity
  - Functional decline (difficulty with stairs, standing, walking, dressing)
  - Suspected fracture, significant prior injury, or progressive deformity
