- If you are on warfarin/another anticoagulant, tell them before any procedures or injections. INR goal and recent values matter (clarify that “3.20” reading).  
- Clarify current BP medication(s) — omeprazole is not for BP, so confirm antihypertensive therapy and adherence.  
- If you have anemia, ask what workup is planned (CBC, iron studies, B12/folate) and whether GI evaluation is needed.

