2) Questions to ask Dr. Lee about type 2 diabetes management
Screening and monitoring
- When was my last HbA1c and what target should we use for me (given my age 52, retinopathy, hypertension)?
- Please order: HbA1c, fasting glucose (if helpful), comprehensive metabolic panel (creatinine/eGFR), urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio, lipid panel, and a recent CBC (for the anemia). Also confirm date of the last retinal exam.
Glycemic targets and therapy
- What HbA1c target do you recommend for me (standard <7.0% vs a higher individualized target) and why?
- Am I on the best class of diabetes medication for my situation? (If not on one already, ask about metformin first-line; if I have ASCVD/high risk or kidney disease, ask whether an SGLT2 inhibitor or GLP‑1 receptor agonist would help.)
