- Significant deformity or instability of a joint
- Severe pain at rest or night pain not responding to meds/therapy
- Failed conservative treatment (physical therapy, activity modification, injections, bracing) after 6–12 weeks
- Imaging (X‑ray, MRI) shows advanced osteoarthritis or other structural problem that may need surgical evaluation
- Acute injury or suspected fracture

