- Given my retinopathy and any neuropathy, am I at increased fall risk that suggests orthopedics or PT evaluation?

What your PCP can do
- Order plain X‑rays of the painful joint or spine if structural disease is suspected.
- Order DEXA if appropriate for bone health.
- Start or refer to physical therapy, pain management, or orthopedics depending on exam/imaging.
- Refer to Northwest Orthopedics if imaging shows advanced arthritis, fracture risk, or if conservative management has failed.

Other annual items to review with Dr. Lee
- Confirm all current medications (names, doses, and reasons) and any over‑the‑counter supplements.
- Review blood pressure targets and home BP monitoring plan.
- Reassess anemia labs (CBC, iron studies, B12, folate) and management.
- Eye care: ensure retinal specialist follow-up given your history of retinopathy.
- Immunizations and cancer screening (age‑appropriate).
- Fall risk assessment and home safety if vision or neuropathy increases risk.

