Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
I can help — this is a good set of things to prepare before your annual physical. A few quick clarifying points first so I give the most accurate suggestions:

- Do you already have a diagnosis of type 2 diabetes? If so, what is your most recent A1c (and date)?  
- Are you taking any diabetes medications now (metformin, insulin, SGLT2, GLP-1, sulfonylurea, etc.)?  
- Are you on any anticoagulant (warfarin) or antiplatelet drug? You wrote “last INR was 320” — did you mean INR = 3.20? (INR is normally ~1.0; 320 looks like a typo.)  
- You wrote “hypertension (omeprazole 20 mg daily)” and “anemia (calcium and vitamin D).” Omeprazole treats acid/GERD, and calcium + vitamin D don’t treat anemia — could you confirm the correct meds/supplements and the conditions they treat?

Once you confirm, I can tailor wording. Meanwhile, here are items and questions you can use for your visit (organized so you can pick what’s most relevant).

Suggested diabetes-related questions to ask your PCP
- Diagnosis and targets
  - Do I have type 2 diabetes (or prediabetes)? What is my current A1c target given my age, comorbidities and retinopathy?
  - What should my target fasting and post‑meal glucose ranges be?
- Monitoring and labs
  - What labs should I have before/at this visit? (A1c, fasting glucose, lipid panel, CMP/creatinine, eGFR, urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio, CBC, vitamin B12 if on metformin)
  - How often should we repeat A1c and urine microalbumin?
- Medications
  - Based on my current labs and risks, should we start or change medications (metformin, SGLT2 inhibitors, GLP‑1 agonists, insulin)?
  - What are the benefits and risks of adding an SGLT2 or GLP‑1 for me (cardio/renal benefits, weight, side effects)? Are there any concerns with my retinopathy or other conditions?
  - Do any diabetes drugs interact with my current medications (omeprazole or any anticoagulants)?
  - Do I need B12 monitoring if on metformin?
- Complication screening & prevention
  - I have a history of retinopathy — when is my next dilated eye exam and who should I see?
  - Should I have baseline neuropathy screening (monofilament, vibration) and a foot exam annually?
  - Do I need earlier or more frequent kidney monitoring because of my age/conditions?
- Hypoglycemia and devices
  - What is my risk of hypoglycemia and how should I manage it? Do I need a glucagon prescription?
  - Should I consider continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) or home glucose checks?
- Cardiovascular & other prevention
  - Do I need an aspirin, statin, or blood pressure medication adjustments because of diabetes?
  - Vaccinations (flu, shingles, pneumococcal) — are any due?
- Lifestyle & referrals
  - Can you refer me to diabetes self‑management education or a dietitian?
  - Any recommended physical activity goals or a structured program?

Questions about referral to Northwest Orthopedics (or any orthopedics)
- Symptoms that warrant referral
  - I’m 52 — do my joint symptoms (describe pain, location, severity, limit to daily activity) merit an orthopedic referral?
  - Should I be referred if I have: persistent pain >3 months, difficulty with walking/stairs, repeated falls, progressive loss of function, or suspected structural injury?
- Diagnostics & conservative care first
  - Would you want plain X‑rays or an MRI before referral?
  - Should I try a course of physical therapy, supervised exercise, weight management, or joint injections first? How long before we consider surgical opinion?
- Bone health and surgery considerations
  - Should I have a DEXA scan given age and calcium/vitamin D use?
  - If I’m on anticoagulation (if applicable), how would that affect timing/risks of any procedure?
- Specialist coordination
  - If I do see Northwest Orthopedics, can you send a referral and include my relevant labs and imaging? Should I see them for elective surgical planning vs. urgent issues?

Pre‑visit checklist (labs and items to bring)
- Updated medication list (prescription, OTC, supplements and doses) and allergy list
- Home blood pressure log (if you monitor at home)
- Recent labs if available (A1c, lipids, CMP, CBC, urine ACR, INR)
- Note symptoms: joint pain (where, how long, what makes worse/better), falls, vision changes
- Ask for these labs if not done recently: A1c, fasting glucose, lipid panel, CMP (creatinine, electrolytes), urine albumin/creatinine, CBC, vitamin B12 (if metformin), INR (if on warfarin), DEXA if indicated
- Bring a list of specific questions you want answered (I can format this into a one‑page checklist)

Other points to mention to Dr. Lee
- Your retinopathy history (makes eye follow‑up important) and any recent vision changes
- Any mobility or balance problems or recent falls — these increase urgency for an ortho/PT evaluation
- Any anticoagulation/bleeding history (important for referral and imaging choices)
- Any current symptoms related to diabetes control (excess thirst, urination, neuropathy symptoms, slow wound healing)

Would you like me to:
- Draft a succinct message/email to Dr. Jennifer Lee summarizing these questions and asking for recommended labs and a referral if indicated? (If yes, tell me whether you want it formal or conversational and confirm any medication names/doses and the correct INR value.)
- Or create a printable one‑page checklist you can take to the visit?

Tell me how you’d like to proceed and confirm the medication/INR details and whether you have a diabetes diagnosis — I’ll draft the email or checklist next.

