- Update labs: A1c, fasting glucose, lipid panel, creatinine/eGFR, urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio, and my most recent INR (I believe it was 3.20).
- Given my history of retinopathy, confirm when I should have my next ophthalmology visit.
- Review current diabetes medication options (including SGLT2/GLP-1) and whether any changes are appropriate considering my kidney function and cardiovascular risk.
- Discuss whether I need a DEXA scan for bone health.
- I’ve had [briefly mention any joint pain or mobility issues here if present]. Should we try physical therapy or refer me to Northwest Orthopedics? Would imaging be helpful first?

Would you like me to send my current med list and recent lab results before the appointment?

—[Your name]

H. Want me to do anything next?
- I can draft a tailored message/email to Dr. Lee (or a portal message) using your exact med list and lab values.
- I can create a one-page checklist for you to bring to the appointment.
- I can draft specific phrasing for in-person questions if you prefer.

If you answer the clarifying questions above (especially whether you have diabetes now, current diabetes meds, and whether you’re on warfarin), I’ll tailor the suggestions and draft a message you can send to Dr. Lee.

