- To Orthopedics (if PCP agrees to refer): “I’m seeking an evaluation for persistent [knee/hip/back] pain that limits [walking/stairs/etc.]. Could you see me for assessment and discuss non‑surgical vs surgical options? Thanks.”

Safety notes / things to watch for
- If you are on anticoagulation (warfarin), discuss with Dr. Lee before any procedures or imaging that might require stopping/reversing anticoagulation.
- Rapid lowering of blood glucose can sometimes transiently worsen diabetic retinopathy — ask about coordinated care with your ophthalmologist if intensifying therapy.

